      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the maximum possible number of planes that can be determined by 12 points in space, we need to calculate the number of ways to choose 3 points out of 12. This is given by the formula for combinations, which is:\n\nC(n, k) = n! / (k!(n-k)!)\n\nwhere n is the total number of points, k is the number of points needed to define a plane, and \"!\" denotes factorial.\n\nIn this case, n = 12 and k = 3:\n\nC(12, 3) = 12! / (3!(12-3)!)\n= 12! / (3!9!)\n= (12 x 11 x 10 x 9!) / (9 x 8 x 7 x 6 x 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1)\n= (12 x 11 x 10) / (1 x 2 x 3)\n= 220\n\nSo, the maximum possible number of planes that can be determined by 12 points in space is 220.",
